{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1437291-changing-breeds-conflicts-with-other-splats","id":1437291,"title":"Changing Breeds conflicts with other splats?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-27T15:34:21-08:00","id":1437291,"title":"Changing Breeds conflicts with other splats?","content":"Small Foreword: I don't actually have any of the Chronicles books yet, since I'm new to the franchise in general. I'm trying to get them myself, but the one store that would allow me to get them is closed currently thanks to Covid, and money is rather tight right now anyway. As a result, I've been looking at various sites, book reviews and boards for information, including this one and TVTropes, so forgive me if my information is a bit wrong. <br /> <br /> So, I was reading through a review over the Changing Breeds book, and I noted that the races tended to get into conflict quite a bit with not just normal humans and werewolves, but also vampires and mages; they regard humans as prey, and the others as rivals to their dominance, from what I can tell. <br /> <br /> The question is, with the Breeds having rivalries with four of the splats (Mage, Vampire, Werewolf, and Hunter given their hatred of humanity) would they have issues or conflicts with any of the other splats (Geist, Beast, Promethean, Changeling, Demon, and Mummy)? I feel like they would have, with their general sense of superiority and arrogance leading them to fighting with everyone, but I'm not entirely sure, since I can't check the book myself; does anyone an opinion they would like to share?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26691-warden","name":"Warden","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T17:47:46-08:00","id":1437305,"title":"","content":"Changing Breeds is one of the older Chronicles of Darkness (then known as World of Darkness, now usually referred to as 1st edition) books, having been published in 2007. As such I doubt you would find a store that still has a physical copy in stock. However you can get PDFs of pretty much all 1st and 2nd edition Chronicles books from drivethrurpg.com, e.g. the Changing Breeds book is <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/51348/World-of-Darkness-Changing-Breeds\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. You can also get print-on-demand books from DriveThruRPG. Usually this is more expensive (especially for the higher-quality print option), but for whatever reason Changing Breeds PDF actually costs more than the print-on-demand option in my local currency.<br /> <br /> One thing to bear in mind about Chronicles of Darkness is that the world is not set in stone. You can include as many or as few of the splats as you like (personally I like to include them all), and although some of the books suggest a viewpoint that your character might have of the other splats (e.g. Storm Lords from Werewolf are likely to view Sin-Eaters negatively since they look a lot like Claimed who are the Storm Lord's favored prey) the books don't really go to any great length to list out how every splat feels about every other splat. All this is to say, how splat X feels about splat Y in your world should be up to you and your group, and will probably depend a lot more on the particular story you're telling and less on how splat X usually feels about splat Y.<br /> <br /> I just looked over the Changing Breeds book to see if it gives advice on how they might feel about the other splats and it does seem that only Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage are detailed along with how the ferals (the term the Changing Breeds book uses for shapechangers) view spirits, humans, and more generic horrors. However it seems that being undead is their big sticking point with Vampires. For that reason, they are likely to take issue with Geists, Mummies, and probably Prometheans. Even if they don't view Prometheans as undead, ferals are supposed to be territorial and so would not appreciate a Promethean messing up their territory with the Disquiet and the Wasteland.<br /> <br /> I find it unlikely that a Demon would reveal itself to ferals, given how xenophobic ferals tend to be. Demons can be nigh impossible for other supernaturals to identify due to the Cover mechanic, so in all likelihood a feral would never know if they were interacting with a Demon.<br /> <br /> Mummies don't tend to care much about other supernaturals unless they have some utility to the Mummy. The most likely source of conflict would be between ferals and the Mummy's human cult - who the ferals would just see as stupid humans doing normal destructive human things. So the most likely interaction would be the cult waking the Mummy for protection, or the ferals breaking into the Mummy's tomb and waking it that way, neither of which are going to end well for the ferals.<br /> <br /> Changelings are a hard one to pin down. Ferals from a prey species might empathise with the Changelings' feeling of always being hunted, while another feral from a predator species might see the Changelings as nothing but cowardly prey. Changelings can be a bit more in tune with nature than most humans (especially the changing of the seasons) and so it's not out of the question that ferals and Changelings could coexist, although it's likely to be a &quot;don't bother us and we won't bother you&quot; sort of arrangement.<br /> <br /> Beasts are supposed to gel easily with other supernaturals and there's no reason to assume this wouldn't extend to ferals too. Personally though I tend to dial back this aspect of Beasts, and so I would probably say that the ferals' dislike of anything &quot;unnatural&quot; would make them highly suspicious of Beasts at the very least. On the other hand, ferals seem unlikely to take issue with how Beasts torment and injure (or even kill) humans to satiate their hunger. The ferals might also see parallels between a &quot;Hero&quot; hunting down a Beast for just being themselves and the way their own species are treated by humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T13:11:28-08:00","id":1437382,"title":"","content":"Beasts automatically make a good first impression on most other supernatural beings unless they do something in particular to offend, but without the right Atavism their relationships can still sour later just as easily as anyone else\u2019s. And considering how incredibly easy it seems to offend a feral even when you\u2019d think they\u2019d get along great with the manifestations of humanity\u2019s animal instincts...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T03:17:40-08:00","id":1437450,"title":"","content":"It should be mentioned that in the Primordial Feast Anthology, Dave wrote a fiction where he detailed his idea for 2e Changing Breed of some kind- and in that story, apparently Beasts <i>don't feel the Ferals</i>. Their Nightmares &quot;slide off them&quot;, because they lack a human soul- instead having a Nahual as a &quot;animal soul&quot;, something which puts them outside of the regular senses of the Begotten.<br /> <br /> Of course, Dave does no longer work for Onyx Path, but still it is the latest thing we have on the Changing Breeds and the most official one we have about their relation with Beasts- and I personally like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-01T04:08:27-08:00","id":1437456,"title":"","content":"I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar503_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"503\" data-vbnamecard=\"503\">LostLight</a>. I think the Changing Breeds in 2e are intended to be more like animal breed Fera from WoD in the sense that they\u2019re not tied that tightly to their human origins and would probably be opposed to a lot of the other supernatural splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}